500, >500); rush vs standard; member vs nonmember; free-delivery threshold check", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, rest at $1.30. Rush adds 0.20*production. Member discount = 0.10*(production+rush) capped at discount-cap; nonmember discount=0. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery=12 unless subtotal-after-discount-and-setup >= 250. Tax=0.08*(subtotal+delivery). Total=round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax).", :operators "pricing compound holds numeric rule parameters but no computation network. struct/slot for output construction. select for branching. +,-,*,/ for arithmetic. min/max for caps. >= for threshold. round-money for final rounding. ttms-premise-closure to attach shared-rule. No existing callable implements the full quote formula.", :outputs "A quote-1 struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total fields, a text reply to user-output-1, and a boolean to self-check-1", :operator "construct a network (e.g. compute-quote) taking quantity, rush?, member?, discount-cap and returning a struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total", :units "dollars for all monetary values, copies for quantity", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-1=80, member-1=false, rush-1=false, discount-cap-1=40, tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08, shared-rule premise available", :decision :construct}, :selected-reference nil, :selected-callable false, :request-count 1, :identity {:id #uuid "0267e58e-a1f1-4204-81b4-73f52a56bfd4", :run-id #uuid "689557d9-59a5-4a7f-9c98-6b5e73055252"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1809bcd7-fb76-330a-8e53-5c65d41ba24a"}} {:round 2, :record {:tests "Self-check verifies: (1) production equals 100*2 + 140*1.60 = 424 (exposes tier arithmetic errors); (2) rush equals 0.20*424 = 84.80 (exposes rush-rate or application errors); (3) discount equals min(0.10*(424+84.80), 40) = 40 (exposes cap logic); (4) subtotal equals (424-40)+25 = 409 (exposes setup-fee placement); (5) delivery equals 0 since 409>=250 (exposes threshold comparison); (6) tax equals 0.08*409 = 32.72 (exposes tax base); (7) total equals round-money(409+0+32.72) = 441.72 (exposes rounding). These are independent arithmetic checks, not re-running the implementation.", :branches "240 copies spans tier-one (100) and tier-two (140), no tier-three. Rush is true so rush-charge applies. Member is true so discount applies but is capped at 40 (raw would be 50.88). Subtotal after discount+setup = 409 >= 250 so delivery is waived.", :rules "Progressive production: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 0.20*production. Member discount = 0.10*(production+rush), capped at discount-cap. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250, else $12. Tax = 0.08*(subtotal+delivery). Total = round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax). Only final total is rounded.", :operators "compute-quote [known, callable]: network [qty rush? member? dcap] -> struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Handles progressive tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, and rounding. Directly matches all requirements for this order. No other pricing callables exist.", :outputs "A quote struct (production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total) connected to quote-2 slots, a formatted text reply to user-output-2, and a boolean self-check to self-check-2.", :operator "compute-quote", :units "Dollars for all monetary values; copies for quantity; rates are dimensionless multipliers.", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-2=240, rush-2=true, member-2=true, discount-cap-2=40. Shared rules: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08. compute-quote is a known callable network [qty rush? member? dcap] returning a struct with all seven slots.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "7f54cf72-84f4-39eb-997b-7038541392e3"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 3, :identity {:id #uuid "0267e58e-a1f1-4204-81b4-73f52a56bfd4", :run-id #uuid "689557d9-59a5-4a7f-9c98-6b5e73055252"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1809bcd7-fb76-330a-8e53-5c65d41ba24a"}} {:round 3, :record {:tests "Self-check verifies structural invariants: subtotal equals (production - discount) + setup-fee; delivery equals select(subtotal>=250, 0, 12); tax equals 0.08*(subtotal+delivery); total equals round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax); production equals 100*2 + 400*1.60 + 220*1.30 (explicit tier arithmetic for 720); rush equals 0; discount equals min(0.10*production, 40). These catch tier-boundary errors, wrong cap application, missing setup, wrong delivery threshold, and rounding placement.", :branches "Standard service: rush-charge=0. Member: discount applies (capped). 720 copies spans all three tiers. Subtotal after discount+setup will exceed 250 so delivery=0.", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush) capped at order discount-cap. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal >= 250. Tax 8% on subtotal+delivery. Final total rounded half-up to cents; intermediates not rounded.", :operators "compute-quote [known, callable]: network [qty rush? member? dcap] -> struct with all seven slots; handles progressive tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, rounding. Suitable for all three rounds. No other pricing callables exist.", :outputs "A quote struct (quote-3) with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total, a text reply to user-output-3, and a boolean to self-check-3", :operator "compute-quote", :units "USD, copies", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-3=720, rush-3=false (standard), member-3=true, discount-cap-3=40; tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, free-delivery-threshold=250, delivery-fee=12, tax-rate=0.08", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "7f54cf72-84f4-39eb-997b-7038541392e3"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 5, :identity {:id #uuid "0267e58e-a1f1-4204-81b4-73f52a56bfd4", :run-id #uuid "689557d9-59a5-4a7f-9c98-6b5e73055252"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1809bcd7-fb76-330a-8e53-5c65d41ba24a"}} {:round 4, :record {:tests "Independent structural checks: (1) production = 90*tier-one-price since 90<tier-one-limit; (2) rush = rush-rate*production; (3) discount = min(member-rate*(production+rush), discount-cap-4); (4) subtotal = (production-discount)+setup-fee; (5) delivery = delivery-fee since subtotal<free-delivery-threshold; (6) tax = tax-rate*(subtotal+delivery); (7) total = round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax). These verify formula structure without reusing compute-quote internals, catching tier misapplication, missing rush, wrong discount cap, wrong delivery branch, or rounding errors.", :branches "90<tier-one-limit so only tier-one applies; rush=true so rush charge applies; member=true so discount applies; subtotal likely <250 so delivery fee applies", :rules "Progressive tiers: 90<100 so all at tier-one-price. Rush adds rush-rate*production. Member discount = min(member-rate*(production+rush), discount-cap). Subtotal = (production-discount)+setup-fee. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250, else delivery-fee. Tax = tax-rate*(subtotal+delivery). Total = round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax).", :operators "compute-quote [known]: network taking [qty rush? member? dcap], returns struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total; handles all tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, rounding. Directly suitable for this input set.", :outputs "Quote breakdown for 90 copies (rush, member): production, rush charge, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, final total; user-facing text; self-check boolean", :operator "compute-quote", :units "dollars and cents; quantities in copies", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-4=90, rush-4=true, member-4=true, discount-cap-4=40; tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "7f54cf72-84f4-39eb-997b-7038541392e3"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 7, :identity {:id #uuid "0267e58e-a1f1-4204-81b4-73f52a56bfd4", :run-id #uuid "689557d9-59a5-4a7f-9c98-6b5e73055252"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1809bcd7-fb76-330a-8e53-5c65d41ba24a"}} {:round 5, :record {:tests "Independent check: (1) production = 100*2 + 400*1.60 + 220*1.30 = 1126 (verifies tier split for 720); (2) rush = 0.20*1126 = 225.20; (3) raw discount = 0.10*(1126+225.20) = 135.12, capped to min(135.12,75)=75 (verifies promotional cap binds); (4) subtotal = (1126-75)+25 = 1076; (5) delivery = 0 since 1076>=250; (6) tax = 0.08*1076 = 86.08; (7) total = round-money(1076+0+86.08) = 1162.08. These checks use explicit arithmetic independent of compute-quote internals and would catch tier miscount, wrong cap, missing setup, wrong delivery branch, or premature rounding.", :branches "720>100+400 so all three tiers apply. rush?=true so rush charge applies. member?=true so discount applies, capped at 75. Subtotal after discount+setup will be well above 250 so delivery=0.", :rules "Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remaining 220 at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush), capped at discount-cap (here $75). Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250. Tax 8% on subtotal+delivery. Round only final total.", :operators "compute-quote [qty rush? member? dcap] — fully implements the pricing pipeline with progressive tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, and rounding. Accepts dcap as parameter so the promotional $75 cap is handled by passing discount-cap-5. No other callable needed.", :outputs "A quote struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total for order-5, a text reply to user-output-5, and a boolean to self-check-5", :operator "compute-quote", :units "dollars and cents; quantities in copies", :unknowns "none", :facts "quantity-5=720, rush-5=true, member-5=true, discount-cap-5=75 (promotional, raised from default 40). Shared rules: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, free-delivery-threshold=250, delivery-fee=12, tax-rate=0.08", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "7f54cf72-84f4-39eb-997b-7038541392e3"}, :selected-callable true, :request-count 9, :identity {:id #uuid "0267e58e-a1f1-4204-81b4-73f52a56bfd4", :run-id #uuid "689557d9-59a5-4a7f-9c98-6b5e73055252"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1809bcd7-fb76-330a-8e53-5c65d41ba24a"}}], :requests [{:id "analysis-1", :text "# Live environment\n\n## phase\nanalysis\n\n## analysis-record\nNo analysis has been submitted for this question yet.\n\n## errors\n[]\n\n## role-cell\nWork carefully from the problem and available facts. Follow the strict procedure and the response format for the current phase. The implementation source is admitted into one persistent lexical child.\n\n## procedure-cell\nStrict procedure, used on its own in this experiment. ANALYSIS phase: First inspect errors, the current structured diagnostic snapshot from earlier implementations. Explain relevant diagnostics and any intended repair in :tests and :operators. Unknown alone does not prove an error. Source references identify actions to inspect, not necessarily causes. Runtime input edges and supports are observations, not proof of causality. You may repair earlier work in the next implementation, and should verify both earlier and current cases. There are no extra repair requests. Before constructing a solution, (1) ground the problem: identify requested outputs, supplied facts, unknowns, units, applicable rules and relevant branches; (2) inspect available bindings and earlier source for relevant callable operators, checking parameters, outputs, assumptions and dependencies rather than names alone; (3) choose an approach: use a suitable existing operator with the current inputs; if none fits, explain the gap and decide whether to adapt an operator or construct one with explicit parameters. Return a concise structured analysis and operator-selection record. Do not implement yet. IMPLEMENTATION phase: implement the recorded approach, using the current inputs. Test it against the original rules with checks capable of exposing a mistake; repeating the implementation arithmetic is not an independent check. Keep new callable operators available. This procedure does not prescribe task-specific formulas or which operator to create.\n\n## output-format-cell\nRead phase first. In analysis phase, return ONLY one EDN map, no Markdown or executable forms, with nonempty string fields :outputs :facts :unknowns :units :rules :branches :operators :operator :tests, plus :decision equal to :reuse, :adapt, or :construct. Use \"none\" for unknowns or operator when appropriate. :operators must summarize the candidates actually available and their suitability. :operator names the selected existing callable for reuse/adapt or proposed new callable for construct. :tests describes independent tests and what mistakes they could detect. The host checks record completeness and existence of selected reuse/adapt callables, not the correctness of your analysis. In implementation phase, analysis-record contains your unchanged analysis. Return executable Lain source only, without fences. Existing parent ports must be connected, not redefined. order-N and pricing are input structs; quote-N has :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Connect the computed breakdown to those slots, a text reply to user-output-N, and your test outcome to self-check-N. N is the current round. Use Lain operations on inputs, not precomputed answer constants. Only final total is rounded to cents.\n\n## context-cell\nOne worker and lexical child remain alive throughout the questions. Earlier definitions remain available in the binding directory. written-code and history contain actual prior source and user/reply messages. Return new forms for the current ask. You may construct test cases or consistency checks using the available operators and connect a boolean result to self-check-N. The parent supplies no quote formula or solved example.\n\n## language-cell\n(define name expression) binds a cell. (network [parameters] body) creates a callable. A network body can contain local define forms and return its final expression, including a struct. (struct :key value ...) constructs connected fields. Read a field with ((slot :key) object). Write an existing field with (-> computed-value ((slot :key) output-object)). + - * / min max >= <= = str and round-money are support-aware operations. (select condition then-value else-value) selects a branch. round-money rounds to two decimals, half up; use it only on the final amount. str builds text from connected values. Unknown inputs leave dependent computations unresolved. ttms-premise-closure attaches a premise to a callable; invocation carries it to results. Example: (define f (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) some-premise)). inspect:premises accepts (cell:reference binding). The struct operators and primitive documentation are capabilities, not prebuilt pricing solutions.\n\n## rules-cell\nFictional print-shop rules: progressive production pricing: first tier-one-limit copies at tier-one-price each; next tier-two-count copies at tier-two-price each; remaining copies at tier-three-price each. Rush service adds rush-rate times production cost. Members receive member-rate times production plus rush charges as discount, capped by the order discount-cap; nonmembers receive no discount. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery costs delivery-fee, waived when subtotal after discount and setup is at least free-delivery-threshold. Apply tax-rate to the entire amount including delivery. Final total includes tax and is rounded half up to cents; intermediate values are not rounded.\n\n## metadata-cell\npricing exposes the shared numeric rules. Every order-N contains independently supported :quantity, :rush? boolean, :member? boolean, :discount-cap, and :question premise. question premises identify the corresponding requested quote. shared-rule identifies the validity premise for the general pricing rules. Keep independent orders separate. A promotional discount-cap belongs only to the order carrying it. delivery-note is unrelated. Quote output slots are production cost, rush charge, discount amount, subtotal after setup, delivery charge, tax amount, and final rounded total. Future orders are unknown until asked.\n\n## ask\nQuote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\n\n## written-code\n[]\n\n## history\n[{:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\"}]\n\n## Binding directory\n- inspect:premises [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"f3cafb7e-9825-334a-9404-100d70bcc84b\"}\n- cell:reference [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids