up = 409 >= 250 so delivery is waived.\"\n :operators \"compute-quote [known, callable]: network [qty rush? member? dcap] -> struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Handles progressive tiers, rush, member discount with cap, setup, delivery threshold, tax, and rounding. Directly matches all requirements for this order. No other pricing callables exist.\"\n :operator \"compute-quote\"\n :tests \"Self-check verifies: (1) production equals 100*2 + 140*1.60 = 424 (exposes tier arithmetic errors); (2) rush equals 0.20*424 = 84.80 (exposes rush-rate or application errors); (3) discount equals min(0.10*(424+84.80), 40) = 40 (exposes cap logic); (4) subtotal equals (424-40)+25 = 409 (exposes setup-fee placement); (5) delivery equals 0 since 409>=250 (exposes threshold comparison); (6) tax equals 0.08*409 = 32.72 (exposes tax base); (7) total equals round-money(409+0+32.72) = 441.72 (exposes rounding). These are independent arithmetic checks, not re-running the implementation.\"\n :decision :reuse}\n\n## errors\n[{:support #{}, :name \"observed-production-1\", :value :unknown, :evidence :runtime-state-and-direct-input-edges, :inputs #{#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"03e95c36-bb27-3d2c-84d1-d5be3637bd65\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"3b90b05b-5d5d-3ab9-82f4-8b34a5dd0ecf\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1b11d-e8c5-7a2b-acf0-44436ee68cfd\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"01a1b11d-e8c2-78c7-88c0-2c7decea8450\"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"24192a08-a3f5-362c-957f-e71467a55f36\"}}, :kind :blocked-output, :source-references [], :meaning \"Inputs and supports come from the runtime. Source references identify uses, not a proven causal action. Unknown can mean waiting for information.\", :cell #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"5e76e776-b053-3368-bfef-56218ea72536\"}} {:support #{}, :name \"observed-rush-1\", :value :unknown, :evidence :runtime-state-and-direct-input-edges, :inputs #{#propagators.ids.NodeId