any intended repair in :tests and :operators. Unknown alone does not prove an error. Source references identify actions to inspect, not necessarily causes. Runtime input edges and supports are observations, not proof of causality. You may repair earlier work in the next implementation, and should verify both earlier and current cases. There are no extra repair requests. Before constructing a solution, (1) ground the problem: identify requested outputs, supplied facts, unknowns, units, applicable rules and relevant branches; (2) inspect available bindings and earlier source for relevant callable operators, checking parameters, outputs, assumptions and dependencies rather than names alone; (3) choose an approach: use a suitable existing operator with the current inputs; if none fits, explain the gap and decide whether to adapt an operator or construct one with explicit parameters. Return a concise structured analysis and operator-selection record. Do not implement yet. IMPLEMENTATION phase: implement the recorded approach, using the current inputs. Test it against the original rules with checks capable of exposing a mistake; repeating the implementation arithmetic is not an independent check. Keep new callable operators available. This procedure does not prescribe task-specific formulas or which operator to create.\n\n## output-format-cell\nRead phase first. In analysis phase, return ONLY one EDN map, no Markdown or executable forms, with nonempty string fields :outputs :facts :unknowns :units :rules :branches :operators :operator :tests, plus :decision equal to :reuse, :adapt, or :construct. Use \"none\" for unknowns or operator when appropriate. :operators must summarize the candidates actually available and their suitability. :operator names the selected existing callable for reuse/adapt or proposed new callable for construct. :tests describes independent tests and what mistakes they could detect. The host checks record completeness and existence of selected reuse/adapt callables, not the correctness of your analysis. In implementation phase, analysis-record contains your unchanged analysis. Return executable Lain source only, without fences. Existing parent ports must be connected, not redefined. order-N and pricing are input structs; quote-N has :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Connect the computed breakdown to those slots, a text reply to user-output-N, and your test outcome to self-check-N. N is the current round. Use Lain operations on inputs, not precomputed answer constants. Only final total is rounded to cents.\n\n## context-cell\nOne worker and lexical child remain alive throughout the questions. Earlier definitions remain available in the binding directory. written-code and history contain actual prior source and user/reply messages. Return new forms for the current ask. You may construct test cases or consistency checks using the available operators and connect a boolean result to self-check-N. The parent supplies no quote formula or solved example.\n\n## language-cell\n(define name expression) binds a cell. (network [parameters] body) creates a callable. A network body can contain local define forms and return its final expression, including a struct. (struct :key value ...) constructs connected fields. Read a field with ((slot :key) object). Write an existing field with (-> computed-value ((slot :key) output-object)). + - * / min max >= <= = str and round-money are support-aware operations. (select condition then-value else-value) selects a branch. round-money rounds to two decimals, half up; use it only on the final amount. str builds text from connected values. Unknown inputs leave dependent computations unresolved. ttms-premise-closure attaches a premise to a callable; invocation carries it to results. Example: (define f (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) some-premise)). inspect:premises accepts (cell:reference binding). The struct operators and primitive documentation are capabilities, not prebuilt pricing solutions.\n\n## rules-cell\nFictional print-shop rules: progressive production pricing: first tier-one-limit copies at tier-one-price each; next tier-two-count copies at tier-two-price each; remaining copies at tier-three-price each. Rush service adds rush-rate times production cost. Members receive member-rate times production plus rush charges as discount, capped by the order discount-cap; nonmembers receive no discount. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery costs delivery-fee, waived when subtotal after discount and setup is at least free-delivery-threshold. Apply tax-rate to the entire amount including delivery. Final total includes tax and is rounded half up to cents; intermediate values are not rounded.\n\n## metadata-cell\npricing exposes the shared numeric rules. Every order-N contains independently supported :quantity, :rush? boolean, :member? boolean, :discount-cap, and :question premise. question premises identify the corresponding requested quote. shared-rule identifies the validity premise for the general pricing rules. Keep independent orders separate. A promotional discount-cap belongs only to the order carrying it. delivery-note is unrelated. Quote output slots are production cost, rush charge, discount amount, subtotal after setup, delivery charge, tax amount, and final rounded total. Future orders are unknown until asked.\n\n## ask\nFor this order only, a promotion raises the member discount cap to $75. Quote 720 copies for a member using rush service. All other rules stay unchanged. Show the charges and final total.\n\n## written-code\n[\"\\n\\n(define compute-quote\\n  (ttms-premise-closure\\n    (network [qty rush? member? dcap]\\n      (define tier-one-copies (min qty tier-one-limit))\\n      (define tier-two-copies (min (max (- qty tier-one-limit) 0) tier-two-count))\\n      (define tier-three-copies (max (- qty tier-one-limit tier-two-count) 0))\\n      (define production (+ (* tier-one-copies tier-one-price)\\n                            (* tier-two-copies tier-two-price)\\n                            (* tier-three-copies tier-three-price)))\\n      (define rush-charge (select rush? (* rush-rate production) 0))\\n      (define raw-discount (select member? (* member-rate (+ production rush-charge)) 0))\\n      (define discount (min raw-discount dcap))\\n      (define subtotal (+ (- production discount) setup-fee))\\n      (define delivery (select (>= subtotal free-delivery-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n      (define tax (* tax-rate (+ subtotal delivery)))\\n      (define total (round-money (+ subtotal delivery tax)))\\n      (struct :production production :rush rush-charge :discount discount :subtotal subtotal :delivery delivery :tax tax :total total))\\n    shared-rule))\\n\\n(define quote-result-1 (compute-quote quantity-1 rush-1 member-1 discount-cap-1))\\n\\n(-> ((slot :production) quote-1) ((slot :production) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) quote-1) ((slot :rush) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) quote-1) ((slot :discount) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) quote-1) ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) quote-1) ((slot :delivery) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) quote-1) ((slot :tax) quote-result-1))\\n(-> ((slot :total) quote-1) ((slot :total) quote-result-1))\\n\\n(-> user-output-1\\n  (str \\\"Quote for \\\" quantity-1 \\\" copies (standard, nonmember):\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Production: $\\\" ((slot :production) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Rush charge: $\\\" ((slot :rush) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Discount: $\\\" ((slot :discount) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Subtotal (incl. setup): $\\\" ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Delivery: $\\\" ((slot :delivery) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Tax: $\\\" ((slot :tax) quote-result-1) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Total: $\\\" ((slot :total) quote-result-1)))\\n\\n(-> self-check-1\\n  (let [prod ((slot :production) quote-result-1)\\n        rush ((slot :rush) quote-result-1)\\n        disc ((slot :discount) quote-result-1)\\n        sub ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-1)\\n        del ((slot :delivery) quote-result-1)\\n        tax ((slot :tax) quote-result-1)\\n        tot ((slot :total) quote-result-1)]\\n    (and (= sub (+ (- prod disc) setup-fee))\\n         (= del (select (>= sub free-delivery-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n         (= tax (* tax-rate (+ sub del)))\\n         (= tot (round-money (+ sub del tax)))\\n         (= prod (* quantity-1 tier-one-price))\\n         (= rush 0)\\n         (= disc 0))))\" \"\\n\\n(define quote-result-2 (compute-quote quantity-2 rush-2 member-2 discount-cap-2))\\n\\n(-> ((slot :production) quote-2) ((slot :production) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) quote-2) ((slot :rush) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) quote-2) ((slot :discount) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) quote-2) ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) quote-2) ((slot :delivery) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) quote-2) ((slot :tax) quote-result-2))\\n(-> ((slot :total) quote-2) ((slot :total) quote-result-2))\\n\\n(-> user-output-2\\n  (str \\\"Quote for \\\" quantity-2 \\\" copies (rush, member):\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Production: $\\\" ((slot :production) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Rush charge: $\\\" ((slot :rush) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Discount: $\\\" ((slot :discount) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Subtotal (incl. setup): $\\\" ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Delivery: $\\\" ((slot :delivery) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Tax: $\\\" ((slot :tax) quote-result-2) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Total: $\\\" ((slot :total) quote-result-2)))\\n\\n(-> self-check-2\\n  (let [prod ((slot :production) quote-result-2)\\n        rush ((slot :rush) quote-result-2)\\n        disc ((slot :discount) quote-result-2)\\n        sub ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-2)\\n        del ((slot :delivery) quote-result-2)\\n        tax ((slot :tax) quote-result-2)\\n        tot ((slot :total) quote-result-2)]\\n    (and (= prod (+ (* tier-one-limit tier-one-price) (* (- quantity-2 tier-one-limit) tier-two-price)))\\n         (= rush (* rush-rate prod))\\n         (= disc (min (* member-rate (+ prod rush)) discount-cap-2))\\n         (= sub (+ (- prod disc) setup-fee))\\n         (= del (select (>= sub free-delivery-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n         (= tax (* tax-rate (+ sub del)))\\n         (= tot (round-money (+ sub del tax))))))\" \"\\n\\n(define quote-result-3 (compute-quote quantity-3 rush-3 member-3 discount-cap-3))\\n\\n(-> ((slot :production) quote-3) ((slot :production) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) quote-3) ((slot :rush) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) quote-3) ((slot :discount) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) quote-3) ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) quote-3) ((slot :delivery) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) quote-3) ((slot :tax) quote-result-3))\\n(-> ((slot :total) quote-3) ((slot :total) quote-result-3))\\n\\n(-> user-output-3\\n  (str \\\"Quote for \\\" quantity-3 \\\" copies (standard, member):\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Production: $\\\" ((slot :production) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Rush charge: $\\\" ((slot :rush) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Discount: $\\\" ((slot :discount) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Subtotal (incl. setup): $\\\" ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Delivery: $\\\" ((slot :delivery) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Tax: $\\\" ((slot :tax) quote-result-3) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Total: $\\\" ((slot :total) quote-result-3)))\\n\\n(-> self-check-3\\n  (let [prod ((slot :production) quote-result-3)\\n        rush ((slot :rush) quote-result-3)\\n        disc ((slot :discount) quote-result-3)\\n        sub ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-3)\\n        del ((slot :delivery) quote-result-3)\\n        tax ((slot :tax) quote-result-3)\\n        tot ((slot :total) quote-result-3)]\\n    (and (= prod (+ (* 100 tier-one-price) (* 400 tier-two-price) (* 220 tier-three-price)))\\n         (= rush 0)\\n         (= disc (min (* member-rate prod) discount-cap-3))\\n         (= sub (+ (- prod disc) setup-fee))\\n         (= del (select (>= sub free-delivery-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n         (= tax (* tax-rate (+ sub del)))\\n         (= tot (round-money (+ sub del tax))))))\" \"\\n\\n(define quote-result-4 (compute-quote quantity-4 rush-4 member-4 discount-cap-4))\\n\\n(-> ((slot :production) quote-4) ((slot :production) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) quote-4) ((slot :rush) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) quote-4) ((slot :discount) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) quote-4) ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) quote-4) ((slot :delivery) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) quote-4) ((slot :tax) quote-result-4))\\n(-> ((slot :total) quote-4) ((slot :total) quote-result-4))\\n\\n(-> user-output-4\\n  (str \\\"Quote for \\\" quantity-4 \\\" copies (rush, member):\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Production: $\\\" ((slot :production) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Rush charge: $\\\" ((slot :rush) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Discount: $\\\" ((slot :discount) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Subtotal (incl. setup): $\\\" ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Delivery: $\\\" ((slot :delivery) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Tax: $\\\" ((slot :tax) quote-result-4) \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"  Total: $\\\" ((slot :total) quote-result-4)))\\n\\n(-> self-check-4\\n  (let [prod ((slot :production) quote-result-4)\\n        rush ((slot :rush) quote-result-4)\\n        disc ((slot :discount) quote-result-4)\\n        sub ((slot :subtotal) quote-result-4)\\n        del ((slot :delivery) quote-result-4)\\n        tax ((slot :tax) quote-result-4)\\n        tot ((slot :total) quote-result-4)]\\n    (and (= prod (* quantity-4 tier-one-price))\\n         (= rush (* rush-rate prod))\\n         (= disc (min (* member-rate (+ prod rush)) discount-cap-4))\\n         (= sub (+ (- prod disc) setup-fee))\\n         (= del (select (>= sub free-delivery-threshold) 0 delivery-fee))\\n         (= tax (* tax-rate (+ sub del)))\\n         (= tot (round-money (+ sub del tax))))))\"]\n\n## history\n[{:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 720 copies for a member using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 90 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"For this order only, a promotion raises the member discount cap to $75. Quote 720 copies for a member using rush service. All other rules stay unchanged. Show the charges and final total.\"}]\n\n## Binding directory\n- compute-quote [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"7f54cf72-84f4-39eb-997b-7038541392e3\"}\n- quote-result-1 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"9749b2a5-2ccc-3390-b1a2-7ea1eec3e03c\"}\n- quote-result-2 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"22d6bf66-67d2-31f0-b50b-726858bdf867\"}\n- quote-result-3 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"b18d782e-7033-3a56-b6df-d05936fdd934\"}\n- quote-result-4 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"b5be8722-29ac-3d20-8c