nmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total."} {:role "user", :content "Quote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total."} {:role "user", :content "Quote 720 copies for a member using standard service. Show the charges and final total."} {:role "user", :content "Quote 90 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total."} {:role "user", :content "For this order only, a promotion raises the member discount cap to $75. Quote 720 copies for a member using rush service. All other rules stay unchanged. Show the charges and final total."}], :outcome {:operational-status :completed, :stable-identity true}, :phase-responses [{:kind :reply, :text "\n\n{:outputs \"A quote-1 struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total fields, a text reply to user-output-1, and a boolean to self-check-1\"\n :facts \"quantity-1=80, member-1=false, rush-1=false, discount-cap-1=40, tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08, shared-rule premise available\"\n :unknowns \"none\"\n :units \"dollars for all monetary values, copies for quantity\"\n :rules \"Progressive tiers: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, rest at $1.30. Rush adds 0.20*production. Member discount = 0.10*(production+rush) capped at discount-cap; nonmember discount=0. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery=12 unless subtotal-after-discount-and-setup >= 250. Tax=0.08*(subtotal+delivery). Total=round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax).\"\n :branches \"Tier selection by quantity (<=100, <=500, >500); rush vs standard; member vs nonmember; free-delivery threshold check\"\n :operators \"pricing compound holds numeric rule parameters but no computation network. struct/slot for output construction. select for branching. +,-,*,/ for arithmetic. min/max for caps. >= for threshold. round-money for final rounding. ttms-premise-closure to attach shared-rule. No existing callable implements the full quote formula.\"\n :operator \"construct a network (e.g. compute-quote) taking quantity, rush?, member?, discount-cap and returning a struct with :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total\"\n :tests \"Verify production for 80 copies equals 80*2=160 (all in tier-one). Verify rush=0 for standard. Verify discount=0 for nonmember. Verify subtotal=160+25=185. Verify delivery=12 since 185<250. Verify tax=(185+12)*0.08=15.76. Verify total=round-money(212.76)=212.76. Cross-check by computing total independently: 160+0+0+25+12+15.76=212.76. Also test tier boundary: 100 copies should give 200 production; 101 should give 200+1.60=201.60. Test member discount cap: if discount would exceed cap, use cap.\"\n :decision :construct}", :thinking "Let me analyze this problem carefully.\n\nThe task is to quote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service.\n\nLet me ground the problem:\n\n**Requested outputs:** A quote struct with :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total fields, plus a text reply and self-check.\n\n**Supplied facts:**\n- quantity-1 = 80\n- member-1 = false (nonmember)\n- rush-1 = false (standard service)\n- discount-cap-1 = 40\n- tier-one-limit = 100\n- tier-one-price = 2\n- tier-two-count = 400\n- tier-two-price = 1.60\n- tier-three-price = 1.30\n- rush-rate = 0.20\n- member-rate = 0.10\n- setup-fee = 25\n- delivery-fee = 12\n- free-delivery-threshold = 250\n- tax-rate = 0.08\n- shared-rule premise exists\n- pricing compound exists\n\n**Rules:**\n1. Progressive production pricing: first tier-one-limit (100) copies at tier-one-price (2) each; next tier-two-count (400) copies at tier-two-price (1.60) each; remaining at tier-three-price (1.30) each.\n2. Rush service adds rush-rate × production cost. (Not applicable here since rush=false)\n3. Members receive member-rate × (production + rush) as discount, cap